# Kairos — local development environment.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this template is committed.
#
# The secure feature database's server key half is no longer configured here: it
# is minted per device by the API and released to the signed-in device over
# `GET /devices/key-half`. Nothing about the encrypted database needs local
# setup — sign in and the half is fetched automatically.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "debug" to force verbose logging.
LOG_LEVEL=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Releasing only — not needed to run the app
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `npm run publish` uploads the Squirrel artifacts to GitHub Releases on
# MarriottFRA/kairos. `@electron-forge/publisher-github` reads this variable and
# nothing else, so without it publish fails with "Please set GITHUB_TOKEN in your
# environment". `forge.config.ts` does `import 'dotenv/config'`, so putting the
# token in `.env` (gitignored) is enough — no need to export it in the shell.
#
# Scope: a classic PAT needs `repo`; a fine-grained PAT needs Contents: Read and
# write AND must explicitly list MarriottFRA/kairos among its repositories — a
# fine-grained token minted for another repo will 404 here. See RELEASING.md.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
